claim.claim-text:
(a) a pressure between 0.1 Pascals and 70 Pascals;
(b) a reducing atmosphere comprising between 70% and 99% hydrogen; and
(c) a pressure between 0.1 Pascals and 70 Pascals in a reducing atmosphere comprising between 70% and 99% hydrogen.

(a) a pressure between 0.1 Pascals and 70 Pascals;
(b) a reducing atmosphere comprising between 70% and 99% hydrogen; and
(c) a pressure between 0.1 Pascals and 70 Pascals in a reducing atmosphere comprising between 70% and 99% hydrogen.

a semiconductor substrate comprising two major, generally parallel surfaces, one of which is the front surface of the semiconductor substrate and the other of which is a back surface of the semiconductor substrate, a circumferential edge joining the front and back surfaces, and a central plane between the front and back surfaces, wherein the semiconductor wafer comprises a material selected from the group consisting of silicon, gallium arsenide, silicon carbide, silicon germanium, germanium, and any combination thereof;
a layer of graphene in contact with the front surface of the semiconductor substrate wherein the layer of graphene in contact with the front surface of the semiconductor substrate comprises a single mono-atomic graphene layer; and
a metal film in contact with the layer of graphene, the metal film comprising a front metal film surface, a back metal film surface, and a bulk metal region between the front and back metal film surfaces.
